<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldSteam.xml                     UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================
  SCALD_MECHANICS_1 build pass, S1 "the boil layer — standing steam"
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/kits/scald_kit_spec.md §S1, the_scald.md
  §9 "cyan glow under white steam"). The Scald's default sky: the boil's own
  breath, not weather-rain — zero precipitation, a standing haze that dulls
  ranged accuracy the way any thick air would, and slows nothing (the sheet
  never asks for a move penalty here; that's Rain's job elsewhere).

  overlayClasses -> RUT_WeatherOverlay_ScaldSteam
  (src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/RUT_WeatherOverlay_ScaldSteam.cs).
  That class's own header explains why this is a Scald-scoped one-off rather
  than the spec's named "RM_WeatherOverlay_GroundFog": that shared class does
  not exist anywhere in the repo (checked), and vanilla's own overlay pattern
  (WeatherOverlay_Fog et al) hardcodes one texture per subclass with no
  XML-configurable texture field, so a literal shared class could not serve
  two different biomes' art anyway. MayRequire-gated: the overlay class and
  RM_GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather (the lock, RUT_ScaldSteamLock.xml)
  both live in mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards.

  accuracyMultiplier 0.9: INVENTED, deliberately milder than Fog's 0.5 — this
  is standing steam over calm water, not a blind. moveSpeedMultiplier 1.0
  (unset/default): the sheet's only traversal penalty is the water's own
  burn, never the air above it. rainRate/snowRate explicit 0: the steam
  layer is presentation, not the R-B rain family (FORGE_MECHANICS_1's own
  scope, not this kit's).

  ambientSounds: Ambient_Wind_Fog reused as-is (real vanilla SoundDef, not
  invented) rather than a bespoke "boil's breath" cue — the sheet's §9 sound
  direction ("the boil's endless breath") is real content the audio/art
  pipeline still owes; this is the nearest already-shipped loop, flagged
  here rather than left silent or given a guessed defName.

  Texture: RUT_WeatherOverlay_ScaldSteam's own hardcoded path
  ("Weather/ScaldSteamOverlayWorld") does not exist under any Textures/
  folder yet — OWED to the art pipeline. Loading with it absent logs an
  error and shows no overlay panner rather than failing to load.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <WeatherDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_ScaldSteam</defName>
    <label>the boil's breath</label>
    <description>Standing white steam over the Scald's cyan boil — the lake's own exhale, thick enough to soften a shot but never enough to slow a step.</description>
    <repeatable>true</repeatable>
    <windSpeedFactor>0.3</windSpeedFactor>
    <accuracyMultiplier>0.9</accuracyMultiplier>
    <rainRate>0</rainRate>
    <snowRate>0</snowRate>
    <favorability>Neutral</favorability>
    <perceivePriority>1</perceivePriority>
    <ambientSounds>
      <li>Ambient_Wind_Fog</li>
    </ambientSounds>
    <overlayClasses>
      <li>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RUT_WeatherOverlay_ScaldSteam</li>
    </overlayClasses>
    <skyColorsDay>
      <sky>(0.86,0.90,0.90)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.90,0.93,0.93)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.75,0.85,0.85)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.85</saturation>
    </skyColorsDay>
    <skyColorsDusk>
      <sky>(0.95,0.92,0.88)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.90,0.90,0.90)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.70,0.78,0.78)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.85</saturation>
    </skyColorsDusk>
    <skyColorsNightEdge>
      <sky>(0.40,0.48,0.50)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.85,0.88,0.88)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.55,0.60,0.60)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.85</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightEdge>
    <skyColorsNightMid>
      <sky>(0.40,0.48,0.50)</sky>
      <shadow>(0.80,0.83,0.83)</shadow>
      <overlay>(0.55,0.60,0.60)</overlay>
      <saturation>0.85</saturation>
    </skyColorsNightMid>
  </WeatherDef>

</Defs>
